// The non-class shape of the same gap. Where a class emitted a call to a vtable that does not exist, a
// plain enum fell through the cascade entirely to `s += val` and passed a raw integer into a struct
// parameter — "passing '_Fx__Color' (aka 'unsigned char') to parameter of incompatible type 'Hashable'".
//
// ⚠️ Not an enum limitation. An enum that DOES implement its contract widens correctly in exactly this
// position — tests/enum_implements.kama passes three of them to `fn isize describe(Error e)` and
// dispatches each to its own impl. What was missing was the check, not the capability.
type enum Color : uint8 { Red, Green, Blue }

fn uint64 hashVia(Hashable h) { return h.hash(); }

fn int32 main()
{
    Color c = Color::Green;
    return cast<int32>(hashVia(h: c));
}
